DSHMap.receive("pkg","@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill-office",{"readme":"# @deepseek-ai/dsh-skill-office\n\nEnglish | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe catalog lists the Office router and six authoring or operation skills. Full instructions load on demand. Authoring skills use the selected Python libraries; operation skills supply the configured Node and LibreOffice Kit CLI paths. SDK and Desktop mount the skill provider and dependency query separately.\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n- [Use this package](#use-this-package)\n  - [Progressive loading](#progressive-loading)\n- [Understand the implementation](#understand-the-implementation)\n- [Further Exploration](#further-exploration)\n- [Model Experience](#model-experience)\n- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)\n- [Dev Note](#dev-note)\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"use-this-package\"></a>\n## Use this package\n\nMount the skill provider beside the skill registry and `dsh-tool-skill`. The provider supplies skill instructions; operation skills append absolute interpreter and CLI paths when loaded.\n\n```yaml\n- name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill-office'\n\n```\n\n| Field | Default | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `assetRoot` | Carrier resources or packaged `assets/` | Absolute directory containing the seven skill folders. |\n| `node` | Host Node.js | Standalone Node executable for operation skills; packaged carriers supply it explicitly. |\n| `cli` | Installed Kit CLI | Absolute CLI entry; `false` disables operation execution. |\n\nInvalid skill assets reject registration. Authoring instructions do not resolve renderer paths; loading operation instructions validates existing interpreter and CLI files without preparing engines. Bash or PowerShell owns approvals, sandboxing, cancellation, and output management. Resources and execution tools must refer to the same host.\n\n<a id=\"progressive-loading\"></a>\n### Progressive loading\n\nThe model chooses skills from the task; the host does not inject complete instructions based on file extensions. All seven skills are listed and loadable by name through `skill` or explicit user invocation. Requested appearance changes, including spreadsheet cell fills and text alignment, require rendering even without an explicit visual-check request; an explicit request to skip rendering takes precedence. Pure operations can enter the corresponding skill directly.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[\"Initial catalog: seven Office summaries\"]\n    A -->|Non-Office task| N[\"Continue without loading Office instructions\"]\n    A -->|Office task| B[\"skill(office): task routing\"]\n\n    B -->|Create or edit| C[\"skill(office-docx / office-pptx / office-xlsx)\"]\n    C --> D[\"Author and validate content, structure and data\"]\n    D -->|No additional operation needed| F[\"Deliver\"]\n\n    B -->|Images, visual inspection, or appearance changes| R[\"skill(office-render)\"]\n    D -->|Images, visual inspection, or appearance changes| R\n    R --> RC[\"Shell: render into a private workspace temporary directory\"]\n    RC -->|Usable preview| V[\"Inspect requested images\"]\n    V --> F\n    RC -->|Failed or blank preview| L[\"Report content checks and unfinished visual inspection separately\"]\n    L --> F\n\n    B -->|Formula recalculation| X[\"skill(office-recalculate)\"]\n    D -->|Formula recalculation| X\n    X --> XC[\"Shell: CLI recalculate and verify values\"]\n    XC --> F\n\n    B -->|PDF export| P[\"skill(office-export-pdf)\"]\n    D -->|PDF export| P\n    P --> PC[\"Shell: CLI convert\"]\n    PC --> F\n```\n\nNew files and content, data, or formula edits do not require rendering solely because they include incidental basic formatting. Preview images use a private, randomly named temporary directory inside the workspace and are removed after inspection; replies report the inspection in text without linking them. PDF export validates the command result and `%PDF-` signature without searching for PDF readers. Loaded instructions remain in session history after an operation finishes. The diagram describes ordinary presets across supported clients; it does not change the shell-only definition of minimal or sdk-minimal.\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"understand-the-implementation\"></a>\n## Understand the implementation\n\n<details>\n<summary>Implementation internals — click to expand</summary>\n\nThe provider reads descriptions at registration and bodies on demand. Registry precedence, scope, and invocation permissions apply to every skill. Each loaded skill includes its resource directory for relative references. Disposal unregisters all candidates.\n\nThe provider registers no tools or activation projection. Loaded skill results remain logged through the generic skill loader. In PTC programs, print or return the full `tools.skill(...)` result so its instructions reach the model. Resume and fork use existing session history and tool declaration reconciliation. Interpreter and CLI paths are resolved only when an operation skill is loaded.\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| [`src/index.ts`](src/index.ts) | Resource registration and unchanged skill bodies. |\n\n| [`assets/`](assets/) | Router and six subskills. |\n\n</details>\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"further-exploration\"></a>\n## Further Exploration\n\n- [Skill registry](../skill/README.md) — discovery and precedence.\n- [Skill tool](../tool-skill/README.md) — model catalogs and loaded bodies.\n- [File delivery](../../deliverables/tool-present/README.md) — current source-path delivery.\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"model-experience\"></a>\n## Model Experience\n\nIndirectly, through `dsh-tool-skill`, which renders the initial Office summary and returns routing or selected subskill instructions from `skill(name)`.\n\n#### KV Cache effect\n\nSkill results append to history without changing tool declarations, and loaded text or images remain after an operation finishes. Character estimates use `ceil(characters / 4)`: the summary is at most 50 tokens and the router body at most 200; authoring bodies are at least 35% smaller than the combined authoring and operation guides. Skill wrappers, the generic catalog, shell declarations, and `load_workspace_dependencies` are separate costs, and these estimates are not server usage.\n\n## Known Limitations and Deferred Work\n\n<a id=\"known-limitations-and-deferred-work\"></a>\n\n- The provider does not install authoring libraries.\n- LibreOffice output can differ from native Office applications.\n- Legacy, encrypted, and macro-enabled files need an appropriate separate workflow.\n\n<a id=\"dev-note\"></a>\n### Dev Note\n\n<details>\n<summary>Working context for maintainers — click to expand</summary>\n\nNone.\n\n</details>\n","modelExperience":"Indirectly, through `dsh-tool-skill`, which renders the initial Office summary and returns routing or selected subskill instructions from `skill(name)`.\n\n#### KV Cache effect\n\nSkill results append to history without changing tool declarations, and loaded text or images remain after an operation finishes. Character estimates use `ceil(characters / 4)`: the summary is at most 50 tokens and the router body at most 200; authoring bodies are at least 35% smaller than the combined authoring and operation guides. Skill wrappers, the generic catalog, shell declarations, and `load_workspace_dependencies` are separate costs, and these estimates are not server usage.","limitations":"- The provider does not install authoring libraries.\n- LibreOffice output can differ from native Office applications.\n- Legacy, encrypted, and macro-enabled files need an appropriate separate workflow.","files":[["README.i18n.yaml",40,1494,"o"],["README.md",136,6619,"o"],["README.zh.md",136,5907,"o"],["assets/office-docx/SKILL.md",40,3725,"o"],["assets/office-export-pdf/SKILL.md",18,1761,"o"],["assets/office-pptx/SKILL.md",64,4415,"o"],["assets/office-recalculate/SKILL.md",18,1723,"o"],["assets/office-render/SKILL.md",31,4841,"o"],["assets/office-xlsx/SKILL.md",52,4579,"o"],["assets/office/SKILL.md",15,957,"o"],["assets/office/references/sidecar.md",17,2510,"o"],["package.json",44,1190,"o"],["src/index.ts",95,4720,"s"],["tests/docx-validation.e2e.ts",70,3894,"t"],["tests/fixtures/encrypted.xlsx",0,224,"t"],["tests/fixtures/real-office.ts",31,1701,"t"],["tests/fixtures/render-cli.ts",61,2846,"t"],["tests/progressive-loading.spec.ts",115,6013,"t"],["tests/render-tools.e2e.ts",131,8416,"t"],["tests/skill-office.spec.ts",208,10382,"t"],["tests/visual-intent.e2e.ts",152,10376,"t"],["tests/xlsx-validation.e2e.ts",235,13611,"t"],["tsconfig.json",24,376,"o"]],"sources":{"README.md":"---\ndescription: \"Progressive Office authoring and CLI operation skills for document workflows.\"\nkind: \"package-reference\"\n---\n\n# @deepseek-ai/dsh-skill-office\n\nEnglish | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe catalog lists the Office router and six authoring or operation skills. Full instructions load on demand. Authoring skills use the selected Python libraries; operation skills supply the configured Node and LibreOffice Kit CLI paths. SDK and Desktop mount the skill provider and dependency query separately.\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n- [Use this package](#use-this-package)\n  - [Progressive loading](#progressive-loading)\n- [Understand the implementation](#understand-the-implementation)\n- [Further Exploration](#further-exploration)\n- [Model Experience](#model-experience)\n- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)\n- [Dev Note](#dev-note)\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"use-this-package\"></a>\n## Use this package\n\nMount the skill provider beside the skill registry and `dsh-tool-skill`. The provider supplies skill instructions; operation skills append absolute interpreter and CLI paths when loaded.\n\n```yaml\n- name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill-office'\n\n```\n\n| Field | Default | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `assetRoot` | Carrier resources or packaged `assets/` | Absolute directory containing the seven skill folders. |\n| `node` | Host Node.js | Standalone Node executable for operation skills; packaged carriers supply it explicitly. |\n| `cli` | Installed Kit CLI | Absolute CLI entry; `false` disables operation execution. |\n\nInvalid skill assets reject registration. Authoring instructions do not resolve renderer paths; loading operation instructions validates existing interpreter and CLI files without preparing engines. Bash or PowerShell owns approvals, sandboxing, cancellation, and output management. Resources and execution tools must refer to the same host.\n\n<a id=\"progressive-loading\"></a>\n### Progressive loading\n\nThe model chooses skills from the task; the host does not inject complete instructions based on file extensions. All seven skills are listed and loadable by name through `skill` or explicit user invocation. Requested appearance changes, including spreadsheet cell fills and text alignment, require rendering even without an explicit visual-check request; an explicit request to skip rendering takes precedence. Pure operations can enter the corresponding skill directly.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[\"Initial catalog: seven Office summaries\"]\n    A -->|Non-Office task| N[\"Continue without loading Office instructions\"]\n    A -->|Office task| B[\"skill(office): task routing\"]\n\n    B -->|Create or edit| C[\"skill(office-docx / office-pptx / office-xlsx)\"]\n    C --> D[\"Author and validate content, structure and data\"]\n    D -->|No additional operation needed| F[\"Deliver\"]\n\n    B -->|Images, visual inspection, or appearance changes| R[\"skill(office-render)\"]\n    D -->|Images, visual inspection, or appearance changes| R\n    R --> RC[\"Shell: render into a private workspace temporary directory\"]\n    RC -->|Usable preview| V[\"Inspect requested images\"]\n    V --> F\n    RC -->|Failed or blank preview| L[\"Report content checks and unfinished visual inspection separately\"]\n    L --> F\n\n    B -->|Formula recalculation| X[\"skill(office-recalculate)\"]\n    D -->|Formula recalculation| X\n    X --> XC[\"Shell: CLI recalculate and verify values\"]\n    XC --> F\n\n    B -->|PDF export| P[\"skill(office-export-pdf)\"]\n    D -->|PDF export| P\n    P --> PC[\"Shell: CLI convert\"]\n    PC --> F\n```\n\nNew files and content, data, or formula edits do not require rendering solely because they include incidental basic formatting. Preview images use a private, randomly named temporary directory inside the workspace and are removed after inspection; replies report the inspection in text without linking them. PDF export validates the command result and `%PDF-` signature without searching for PDF readers. Loaded instructions remain in session history after an operation finishes. The diagram describes ordinary presets across supported clients; it does not change the shell-only definition of minimal or sdk-minimal.\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"understand-the-implementation\"></a>\n## Understand the implementation\n\n<details>\n<summary>Implementation internals — click to expand</summary>\n\nThe provider reads descriptions at registration and bodies on demand. Registry precedence, scope, and invocation permissions apply to every skill. Each loaded skill includes its resource directory for relative references. Disposal unregisters all candidates.\n\nThe provider registers no tools or activation projection. Loaded skill results remain logged through the generic skill loader. In PTC programs, print or return the full `tools.skill(...)` result so its instructions reach the model. Resume and fork use existing session history and tool declaration reconciliation. Interpreter and CLI paths are resolved only when an operation skill is loaded.\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| [`src/index.ts`](src/index.ts) | Resource registration and unchanged skill bodies. |\n\n| [`assets/`](assets/) | Router and six subskills. |\n\n</details>\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"further-exploration\"></a>\n## Further Exploration\n\n- [Skill registry](../skill/README.md) — discovery and precedence.\n- [Skill tool](../tool-skill/README.md) — model catalogs and loaded bodies.\n- [File delivery](../../deliverables/tool-present/README.md) — current source-path delivery.\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"model-experience\"></a>\n## Model Experience\n\nIndirectly, through `dsh-tool-skill`, which renders the initial Office summary and returns routing or selected subskill instructions from `skill(name)`.\n\n#### KV Cache effect\n\nSkill results append to history without changing tool declarations, and loaded text or images remain after an operation finishes. Character estimates use `ceil(characters / 4)`: the summary is at most 50 tokens and the router body at most 200; authoring bodies are at least 35% smaller than the combined authoring and operation guides. Skill wrappers, the generic catalog, shell declarations, and `load_workspace_dependencies` are separate costs, and these estimates are not server usage.\n\n## Known Limitations and Deferred Work\n\n<a id=\"known-limitations-and-deferred-work\"></a>\n\n- The provider does not install authoring libraries.\n- LibreOffice output can differ from native Office applications.\n- Legacy, encrypted, and macro-enabled files need an appropriate separate workflow.\n\n<a id=\"dev-note\"></a>\n### Dev Note\n\n<details>\n<summary>Working context for maintainers — click to expand</summary>\n\nNone.\n\n</details>\n","assets/office-docx/SKILL.md":"---\nname: office-docx\ndescription: Create, read, edit, and validate Word documents (.docx).\n---\n\n# Word documents\n\nUse `python-docx` for DOCX creation and ordinary edits. Follow an explicit user or applicable AGENTS.md requirement for a project environment or another library. Otherwise call `load_workspace_dependencies` and execute the returned Python path with its bundled libraries. Do not install packages or discover a system Python for the default workflow. If the tool is unavailable, use an already configured environment and report a missing dependency only when it prevents the requested operation.\n\nKeep source scripts, intermediate files, and final documents in the task workspace; the runtime and this skill directory are read-only resources. Use the user's requested language and preserve an existing document's design unless a redesign is requested.\n\nName Python scripts for their task, such as `edit_docx.py`; avoid module names such as `inspect.py`, `docx.py`, or `zipfile.py` that shadow imported libraries.\n\n## Create and edit\n\nFor text edits, locate the target by its text or position and inspect only its runs and formatting. A title can be an ordinary paragraph without a Title style or document-property title. Update the relevant runs; assigning paragraph `.text` destroys run formatting. Save a new file unless an in-place edit is requested. Read other structures only when the edit involves them; rebuilding a document can lose unsupported features.\n\nUse paragraph styles for headings and body text. Size tables for the section that contains them, and account for merged cells and nested tables. Chinese, Japanese, and Korean text may need an explicit `w:eastAsia` font assignment in addition to `run.font.name`; font names alone do not establish glyph availability or rendered appearance.\n\nFor a new document, use the selected Python executable:\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\n\ndocument = Document()\ndocument.add_heading(\"Project report\", level=0)\ndocument.add_paragraph(\"Summary\", style=\"Heading 1\")\ndocument.add_paragraph(\"The requested findings go here.\")\ndocument.save(\"report.docx\")\n```\n\npython-docx does not paginate or render documents. Do not represent ordinary replacement, colored text, or comments as tracked changes. When real revisions or unsupported OOXML features matter, preserve their package parts and verify the requested operation rather than silently discarding them. When writing package parts directly, create a new ZIP and copy each unchanged member once; appending a replacement member duplicates its name and corrupts the package.\n\n## Check and deliver\n\nReopen the saved document with python-docx and verify the requested content, related formatting, and unchanged content that must be preserved. Deliver when these checks pass. Investigate package-level details only for a concrete failure, ambiguous edit target, unsupported feature, or explicit user requirement.\n\nCreating a file or changing content with incidental basic formatting does not require additional operations. Load `office-render` for requested images or visual inspection. When styling, font color, spacing, sizing, or text alignment is the requested edit, load `office-render` and inspect the changed page even without a separate visual-check request, unless the user explicitly skips rendering. For PDF output load `office-export-pdf`.\n\nCall `present({\"files\":[{\"path\":\"report.docx\"}]})` with the actual final DOCX path. It exposes the current source file without copying or preserving its bytes, so keep that file in place and do not present temporary QA reports unless requested. If `present` is unavailable, provide the final workspace path using the session's supported file delivery method.\n","assets/office-export-pdf/SKILL.md":"---\nname: office-export-pdf\ndescription: Convert an Office document to a requested PDF with LibreOffice Kit.\n---\n\n# Export an Office document to PDF\n\nUse the installed LibreOffice Kit CLI through the shell with the absolute Node and CLI paths supplied below. In Bash, invoke `\"<node>\" \"<cli>\"`; in PowerShell, invoke `& \"<node>\" \"<cli>\"`. Prefer bundled LibreOffice unless the user requests another installation. If the Office sidecar is missing, follow [sidecar setup](../office/references/sidecar.md): ask whether the user wants to download it and install only after they agree. Do not invoke system soffice, use npx, or install a replacement to work around a failed conversion with an installed sidecar.\n\nConvert the final saved Office file to a new PDF in the task workspace. Preserve the source. Quote each input and output path.\n\n```text\n\"<node>\" \"<cli>\" convert --input <final-office-file> --output <new-file.pdf>\n```\n\nCheck the command result, nonempty output, and `%PDF-` file signature, then report that extent of validation. Unless the user requests deeper checks, do not search for PDF readers, generate images, or install tools to validate a conversion. Spreadsheet PDF pages follow workbook print settings; change those settings only when requested. Conversion may differ from the native application's pagination or fonts.\n\nIf export fails, preserve the usable source and report the export limitation. Do not repeatedly convert an unchanged source or use conversion to investigate a failed preview. For PDF export alone, stop after these checks. Only a request for images or visual inspection calls for `office-render`; load it before that separate operation. Deliver the requested PDF through `present` when available, keeping the file in place.\n","assets/office-pptx/SKILL.md":"---\nname: office-pptx\ndescription: Create, read, edit, and validate PowerPoint presentations (.pptx).\n---\n\n# PowerPoint presentations\n\nFollow an explicit user or applicable AGENTS.md requirement for an environment or library. Otherwise call `load_workspace_dependencies` and use its Python executable and bundled presentation libraries. Do not install npm or pip packages or locate a system interpreter for the default workflow. If the tool is unavailable, use an already configured environment and report a missing dependency only when it prevents the requested operation.\n\nKeep scripts and output files in the task workspace. The runtime and skill directory contain shared read-only resources. Match the requested slide language and the supplied presentation's design when editing it.\n\nName Python scripts for their task, such as `edit_pptx.py`; avoid module names such as `inspect.py`, `pptx.py`, or `zipfile.py` that shadow imported libraries.\n\n## Create and edit\n\nUse `python-pptx` to inspect or modify an existing presentation. Inspect slide layouts, text runs, images, tables, and charts before editing. Change only the requested content, preserve mixed text formatting, and save to a new file unless the user requests an in-place edit. Rebuilding slides can discard unsupported animation, SmartArt, or other extension content.\n\nFor a new deck, use `python-pptx` with editable text, tables, and charts. Use local image assets rather than network-dependent image URLs. Set slide dimensions, text sizes, and chart data explicitly.\n\nA minimal editable deck, run with the selected Python executable:\n\n```python\nfrom pptx import Presentation\nfrom pptx.chart.data import CategoryChartData\nfrom pptx.enum.chart import XL_CHART_TYPE\nfrom pptx.util import Inches, Pt\n\npresentation = Presentation()\npresentation.slide_width = Inches(13.333)\npresentation.slide_height = Inches(7.5)\nslide = presentation.slides.add_slide(presentation.slide_layouts[6])\ntitle = slide.shapes.add_textbox(Inches(0.6), Inches(0.4), Inches(12), Inches(0.8))\nrun = title.text_frame.paragraphs[0].add_run()\nrun.text = \"Quarterly report\"\nrun.font.size = Pt(30)\ndata = CategoryChartData()\ndata.categories = [\"Q1\", \"Q2\"]\ndata.add_series(\"Revenue\", [12, 18])\nslide.shapes.add_chart(XL_CHART_TYPE.COLUMN_CLUSTERED,\n                       Inches(0.8), Inches(1.6), Inches(11.5), Inches(4.8), data)\npresentation.save(\"report.pptx\")\n```\n\nUse `Inches` or `Cm` for positions and sizes and `Pt` for font sizes. To edit a generated title while retaining its other slides and charts:\n\n```python\nfrom pptx import Presentation\n\npresentation = Presentation(\"report.pptx\")\nfor shape in presentation.slides[0].shapes:\n    if shape.has_text_frame and shape.text == \"Quarterly report\":\n        shape.text_frame.paragraphs[0].runs[0].text = \"Quarterly results\"\npresentation.save(\"report-edited.pptx\")\n```\n\nCheck that text and images fit the slide dimensions, titles form a useful sequence, and chart labels agree with source values. Paragraph alignment does not move a text box: when a title must be centered on the slide, center both its paragraph and the text box against `presentation.slide_width`, then reopen to verify both. A native chart's embedded workbook is part of the deliverable and must contain the intended data. Library support for writing PPTX is not a rendering engine or a guarantee that every PowerPoint feature survives editing.\n\n## Check and deliver\n\nReopen the saved presentation with python-pptx to verify the requested slide count, content, formatting, chart data, and notes, including unchanged content that must be preserved. These checks do not establish text fit, readable contrast, or rendering fidelity.\n\nDeliver after the requested edits are verified. Creating a file or changing content with incidental basic formatting does not require additional operations. Load `office-render` for requested images or visual inspection and for appearance-focused styling, spacing, sizing, or alignment changes unless the user explicitly skips rendering. For PDF output load `office-export-pdf`.\n\nCall `present({\"files\":[{\"path\":\"report-edited.pptx\"}]})` with the actual final PPTX path. It exposes the current source file without copying or preserving its bytes, so keep that file in place and leave intermediate images and reports out of delivery unless requested. If `present` is unavailable, use the session's supported file delivery method.\n","assets/office-recalculate/SKILL.md":"---\nname: office-recalculate\ndescription: Refresh spreadsheet formula caches and verify calculated values with LibreOffice Kit.\n---\n\n# Recalculate spreadsheet formulas\n\nUse the installed LibreOffice Kit CLI through the shell with the absolute Node and CLI paths supplied below. In Bash, invoke `\"<node>\" \"<cli>\"`; in PowerShell, invoke `& \"<node>\" \"<cli>\"`. Prefer bundled LibreOffice unless the user requests another installation. If the Office sidecar is missing, follow [sidecar setup](../office/references/sidecar.md): ask whether the user wants to download it and install only after they agree. Do not invoke system soffice, use npx, or install a replacement to work around a failed recalculation with an installed sidecar.\n\nKeep the original workbook and write a new file in the task workspace. Quote each input and output path.\n\n```text\n\"<node>\" \"<cli>\" recalculate --input <workbook.xlsx> --output <recalculated.xlsx>\n```\n\nVerify the saved result with openpyxl, using `load_workspace_dependencies` for the Python path unless a project environment is required. Open it with both `data_only=False` and `data_only=True`. Check that formulas survive and cached results match the requested logic, expected totals, and cell types. Check required unchanged sheets, styles, and data. Recalculation does not validate business logic or guarantee Excel-specific feature compatibility.\n\nIf no supported recalculation engine is available or the command fails, preserve the workbook and explain that calculated values could not be refreshed. Do not replace requested formulas with constants or present stale/absent caches as fresh results. Deliver the verified output through `present` when available, keeping the file in place.\n","assets/office-render/SKILL.md":"---\nname: office-render\ndescription: Render requested document images or inspect visual layout with LibreOffice Kit.\n---\n\n# Document images and visual inspection\n\nUse the installed LibreOffice Kit CLI through the shell with the absolute Node and CLI paths supplied below. In Bash, invoke `\"<node>\" \"<cli>\"`; in PowerShell, invoke `& \"<node>\" \"<cli>\"`. Prefer bundled LibreOffice unless the user requests another installation. If the Office sidecar is missing, follow [sidecar setup](../office/references/sidecar.md): ask whether the user wants to download it and install only after they agree. Do not invoke system soffice, use npx, install a replacement renderer, or build an alternative rendering pipeline to work around a failed render with an installed sidecar.\n\nBefore generating images only for inspection, establish that the current model accepts images. Otherwise finish the applicable content and structure checks and report the requested visual check as unavailable. Do not generate unreadable previews, retry image reads, or choose a second model. Requested image exports can still be delivered.\n\n## Render the saved deliverable\n\nKeep the saved deliverable in the task workspace. For requested image exports, use the requested output directory and retain the images. For inspection-only previews, create a private, uniquely named temporary parent inside that workspace and pass a child path that does not yet exist as `--output-dir`; the CLI creates that child. On POSIX, use `preview_root=$(mktemp -d \"./.dsh-office.XXXXXXXX\")` (owner-only permissions) and `--output-dir \"$preview_root/render\"`. On PowerShell, create a parent named `.dsh-office-` plus `[guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N')` under the task workspace and pass an uncreated `render` child; it inherits the workspace ACL. Quote each input and output path. Retain the parent until image inspection finishes, then remove only that parent, including after a failed render. Never use a fixed directory name or remove the workspace itself. Report inspection results in text; the reply must not link or embed removed previews.\n\n```text\n\"<node>\" \"<cli>\" render --input <final-file> --output-dir <new-directory> --pages \"1,3,4\"\n\"<node>\" \"<cli>\" render --input <final-workbook.xlsx> --output-dir <new-directory> --sheet <exact-name> --range <A1-range>\n```\n\nFor DOCX, PPTX, or PDF, batch requested pages/slides in one call. In PowerShell, quote comma-separated `--pages` values so they remain one argument. Inspect all pages only for a requested whole-document review. For worksheets, choose the exact affected range, including chart/drawing regions; worksheet numbers are not PDF page numbers. Inspect the final saved file, reuse existing images for an unchanged source, and rerender only after requested source changes or for previously unrendered regions. Change print areas or scaling only when the user requests print layout.\n\nRead the returned JSON manifest for image paths, page counts, fragment rectangles, and missing-font diagnostics. Use the session's image-reading tool to inspect the requested images. Check clipping, alignment, headings, table widths, contrast, chart labels, and number formats as relevant to the task. A successful command or image read alone does not establish a usable preview; guessed text geometry does not establish overflow.\n\n## Failed or blank previews\n\nFor populated content, a fully transparent or uniformly blank image is a renderer failure. If a pixel check is needed, composite RGBA onto white first; raw RGB under transparent pixels can look nonblank. Check once and do not reread the same image. Stop visual checks for the task immediately after a blank result. This overrides the rerender-after-edit guidance above: do not render or read images again, even after editing or copying the source, or try another range, page, sheet, DPI, output format, diagnostic export, or print setting. Preserve the usable source and requested outputs and finish applicable content/data checks.\n\nIf content and structure checks pass, name the saved file and verified edits as needed, then include exactly one visual-status sentence: \"Content and structure checks passed; visual inspection was not completed.\" in English, or \"内容与结构检查通过；视觉检查未完成。\" in Chinese. Do not add a render or preview bullet, explain why inspection stopped, or describe the image or pixels. Report content or structure failures separately; never say all checks passed or claim visual verification.\n\nLibreOffice output can differ from Word, PowerPoint, or Excel. Images do not certify animation/media playback, refresh formula caches in the source workbook, or guarantee native application fidelity. Deliver requested files through `present` when available; keep the files in place. Do not deliver inspection images or reports unless requested.\n","assets/office-xlsx/SKILL.md":"---\nname: office-xlsx\ndescription: Read, create, edit, and validate Excel workbooks, data, and formulas (.xlsx).\n---\n\n# Excel workbooks\n\nFollow an explicit user or applicable AGENTS.md requirement for an environment or library. Otherwise call `load_workspace_dependencies` and run its Python executable with bundled `openpyxl` and `pandas`. Do not install packages or search for a system Python for the default workflow. If the tool is unavailable, use an already configured environment and report a missing dependency only when it prevents the requested operation.\n\nKeep scripts, working files, and outputs in the task workspace. The runtime and skill directory are shared read-only resources. Save to a new workbook unless the user requests an in-place edit.\n\nName Python scripts for their task, such as `edit_xlsx.py`; avoid module names such as `inspect.py`, `openpyxl.py`, or `pandas.py` that shadow imported libraries.\n\n## Read and modify\n\nUse `openpyxl` for existing XLSX workbooks and targeted cell or style changes. Load with `data_only=False` when formulas must survive. Inspect sheet names, the affected cell types, formulas, styles, merged ranges, and referenced ranges before editing. Check the saved file by reopening it, including unchanged content that the request requires preserving.\n\nUse pandas for data analysis and transformations. A DataFrame is not the workbook: exporting it over an existing file can lose sheets, formulas, charts, and formatting. Write analysis results back to the intended ranges with openpyxl. `XlsxWriter` can create new workbooks, but cannot read or modify existing ones.\n\nFor a new workbook, the selected Python environment can write editable values, styles, and formulas directly:\n\n```python\nfrom openpyxl import Workbook\nfrom openpyxl.styles import Font\n\nworkbook = Workbook()\nsheet = workbook.active\nsheet.title = \"Revenue\"\nfor row in [(\"Quarter\", \"Revenue\"), (\"Q1\", 12), (\"Q2\", 18), (\"Total\", \"=SUM(B2:B3)\")]:\n    sheet.append(row)\nfor cell in sheet[1]:\n    cell.font = Font(bold=True)\nsheet.column_dimensions[\"A\"].width = 18\nsheet.column_dimensions[\"B\"].width = 18\nworkbook.save(\"report.xlsx\")\n```\n\nPreserve numbers, dates, booleans, and identifiers as the intended cell types; formatting is not a type conversion. For modifications, load the existing file with `openpyxl.load_workbook(\"input.xlsx\", data_only=False)`, change the requested ranges, and save a separate result. Avoid a DataFrame round trip when workbook features must survive.\n\nWriting a formula does not calculate its result. openpyxl and XlsxWriter do not evaluate formulas; `data_only=True` returns cached values that may be absent or stale. When calculated results must be refreshed, load `office-recalculate`. Do not replace requested formulas with constants or report stale values as newly calculated results.\n\nDo not rename `.xls`, `.xlsb`, encrypted files, or macro-enabled files to `.xlsx`. They need an appropriate supported operation. `keep_vba=True` can preserve VBA package content in an XLSM workflow, but does not execute or edit macros and does not guarantee every advanced workbook feature survives. Preserve the original and verify such requirements explicitly.\n\n## Check and deliver\n\nReopen the saved workbook with openpyxl and verify the requested sheet names, values, types, formulas, styles, and totals against the source data, including unchanged content that must be preserved. These checks do not calculate formulas or judge workbook appearance.\n\nLoad `office-render` for requested images or visual inspection and whenever the user's primary task targets appearance, including cell fill colors, text alignment, spacing, or sizing. These appearance changes require rendering even without a separate visual-check request, unless the user explicitly skips it. New workbooks and data or formula edits do not require rendering solely because they include incidental basic formatting. In particular, bold headers and number formats accompanying data edits do not require loading `office-render` or running its commands.\n\nLoad `office-recalculate` when refreshed calculated values are needed and `office-export-pdf` for PDF output. Deliver after the requested data checks pass and the required operations finish.\n\nCall `present({\"files\":[{\"path\":\"report.xlsx\"}]})` with the actual final workbook path. It exposes the current source file without copying or preserving its bytes, so keep that file in place and omit intermediate scripts and reports unless requested. If `present` is unavailable, use the session's supported file delivery method.\n","assets/office/SKILL.md":"---\nname: office\ndescription: Create, edit, inspect, or convert Office documents, spreadsheets, presentations, and PDFs. Load to choose the relevant workflow.\n---\n\n# Office task routing\n\nCall the `skill` tool with the format skill name before creating, reading, or editing Office files. Standalone rendering, PDF export, and recalculation need only their operation skill.\n\n- Create, read, or edit: `office-docx` (Word), `office-pptx` (PowerPoint), or `office-xlsx` (Excel).\n- Images, visual inspection, or tasks primarily about layout, spacing, sizing, or alignment: `office-render`, even without an explicit visual-check request.\n- Refresh spreadsheet formula results: `office-recalculate`.\n- Export an Office file to PDF: `office-export-pdf`.\n\nHonor requests to skip rendering. New files, content edits, formulas, and incidental formatting such as bold headers or number formats need no render unless visual inspection is requested. Do not reload skills.\n","assets/office/references/sidecar.md":"# Missing Office sidecar\n\nThese instructions apply in Web, Desktop, and SDK sessions. First check whether an existing LibreOffice Kit installation can serve the task; a missing `dsoffice` command on PATH alone does not establish that the sidecar is absent. If the required sidecar is missing and the user has not already authorized its download, use the available ask-question tool to ask whether they want to download the Office conversion engine. If that tool is unavailable, ask in the conversation. Wait for explicit agreement before downloading or installing; if the user declines, continue work that does not need the engine and report the unavailable operation.\n\nAfter agreement, install `@deepseek-ai/libreoffice-kit` together with the matching engine package, using the engine version declared by the main package's optional dependencies. Use an available npm or pnpm in a task-local tools directory, with `--ignore-scripts`: the packages provide prebuilt binaries and do not need installation scripts. Keep the package manager's cache or store in that writable task directory too (for npm, pass `--cache <task-tools-directory>/.npm-cache`). Select the package for the operating system and architecture of the Node.js process that will run the CLI, including when Node runs under emulation:\n\n| Runtime platform | Engine package |\n| --- | --- |\n| Windows x64 | `@deepseek-ai/libreoffice-kit-win32-x64` |\n| Windows ARM64 | `@deepseek-ai/libreoffice-kit-win32-arm64` |\n| macOS Apple Silicon | `@deepseek-ai/libreoffice-kit-darwin-arm64` |\n| macOS Intel | `@deepseek-ai/libreoffice-kit-darwin-x64` |\n| No matching native package, including Linux | `@deepseek-ai/libreoffice-kit-wasm` |\n\nPrefer the matching native package; otherwise use WASM when its package supports the current platform. Check package platform restrictions before installation rather than forcing an incompatible package. The published WASM package currently declares Linux support.\n\nReuse the bundled Node.js and pnpm paths from `load_workspace_dependencies` when available, or the user's configured Node.js and package manager. Permission to download the Office sidecar does not include installing Python, Node.js, or a package manager. If those prerequisites are missing, explain what is needed. Run the new installation's `dsoffice` entry, or its `lib/cli.js` with the selected Node executable, by path; do not assume installation changed the session's PATH. Check `dsoffice capabilities` before continuing the requested operation.\n","package.json":"{\n  \"name\": \"@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill-office\",\n  \"description\": \"Bundled Word, PowerPoint, and Excel workflows and LibreOffice Kit operations\",\n  \"version\": \"0.2.1-rc.2\",\n  \"publishConfig\": {\n    \"access\": \"public\"\n  },\n  \"repository\": {\n    \"type\": \"git\",\n    \"url\": \"git+https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness.git\",\n    \"directory\": \"packages/skill/skill-office\"\n  },\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"main\": \"lib/index.js\",\n  \"types\": \"lib/types/index.d.ts\",\n  \"exports\": {\n    \".\": {\n      \"types\": \"./lib/types/index.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./lib/index.js\"\n    },\n    \"./package.json\": \"./package.json\"\n  },\n  \"files\": [\n    \"lib/index.js\",\n    \"assets\",\n    \"lib/types/**/*.d.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"peerDependencies\": {\n    \"@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@deepseek-ai/cordis\": \"workspace:~\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@deepseek-ai/cordis\": \"workspace:~\",\n    \"@deepseek-ai/cordis-plugin-loader\": \"workspace:~\",\n    \"@deepseek-ai/cordis-plugin-include\": \"workspace:~\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@deepseek-ai/libreoffice-kit\": \"^0.1.5\",\n    \"@deepseek-ai/schemastery\": \"workspace:~\",\n    \"yaml\": \"^2.4.2\"\n  }\n}\n","src/index.ts":"/** Bundled Office workflows and filesystem resources for document authoring and operations. */\n\nimport { readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs'\nimport { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises'\nimport { dirname, isAbsolute, join, sep } from 'node:path'\nimport { isSea } from 'node:sea'\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'\nimport type { Context } from '@deepseek-ai/cordis'\nimport z from '@deepseek-ai/schemastery'\nimport { BUNDLED_SKILL_RANK, type SkillCandidate, type SkillProvider } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill'\nimport { parse as parseYaml } from 'yaml'\n\nconst SKILL_NAMES = ['office', 'office-docx', 'office-pptx', 'office-xlsx', 'office-render', 'office-recalculate', 'office-export-pdf'] as const\n\n/** Office skill resource location. */\nexport interface Config {\n  /** Absolute assets directory containing skill folders; defaults to packaged assets. */\n  assetRoot?: string\n  /** Standalone Node executable; defaults to the current executable outside Electron and SEA. */\n  node?: string\n  /** Absolute LibreOffice Kit CLI entry; false explicitly disables CLI access. */\n  cli?: string | false\n}\n\n/** Validated resource configuration. */\nexport const Config: z<Config> = z.object({\n  assetRoot: z.string().min(1),\n  node: z.string().min(1),\n  cli: z.union([z.string().min(1), z.const(false)]),\n})\n\n/** Cordis plugin identity. */\nexport const name = 'skill-office'\n/** Registry used by the bundled provider. */\nexport const inject = ['skills']\n\nfunction parseSkill(raw: string, path: string): { description: string; content: string } {\n  const frontmatter = /^---\\r?\\n([\\s\\S]*?)\\r?\\n---(?:\\r?\\n|$)/u.exec(raw)\n  if (frontmatter?.[1] === undefined) throw new Error(`skill-office: ${path} has no YAML frontmatter`)\n  const metadata: unknown = parseYaml(frontmatter[1])\n  const description = typeof metadata === 'object' && metadata !== null && 'description' in metadata\n    ? metadata.description : undefined\n  if (typeof description !== 'string' || description.length === 0) throw new Error(`skill-office: ${path} has no description`)\n  return { description, content: raw.slice(frontmatter[0].length).trim() }\n}\n\nfunction officeRuntime(config: Config): string {\n  if (config.cli === false) return '\\n\\nLibreOffice Kit is disabled in this deployment.'\n  if (config.node === undefined && (isSea() || process.versions.electron !== undefined)) {\n    throw new Error('skill-office: packaged applications must supply a standalone Node executable')\n  }\n  const node = config.node ?? process.execPath\n  let cli = config.cli\n  if (cli === undefined) {\n    const manifestPath = fileURLToPath(import.meta.resolve('@deepseek-ai/libreoffice-kit/package.json'))\n    cli = join(dirname(manifestPath), 'lib', 'cli.js')\n  }\n  for (const path of [node, cli]) {\n    if (!isAbsolute(path) || !statSync(path).isFile()) throw new Error(`skill-office: expected an absolute executable file: ${path}`)\n  }\n  return `\\n\\n## Installed LibreOffice Kit\\n\\nUse these absolute paths for every LibreOffice Kit command. Pass the CLI entry as the first argument to Node.\\n\\n${JSON.stringify({ libreofficeKit: { node, cli } }, undefined, 2)}`\n}\n\n/**\n * Register Office skills with resources readable by the script interpreter.\n * @param ctx - Context carrying the skill registry.\n * @param config - Optional external assets directory for packaged applications.\n */\nexport function apply(ctx: Context, config: Config = {}): void {\n  const assetRoot = config.assetRoot ?? fileURLToPath(new URL('../assets/', import.meta.url))\n  if (!isAbsolute(assetRoot)) throw new Error('skill-office: assetRoot must be an absolute directory')\n  const candidates: SkillCandidate[] = SKILL_NAMES.map((skillName) => {\n    const directory = join(assetRoot, skillName)\n    const path = join(directory, 'SKILL.md')\n    const { description } = parseSkill(readFileSync(path, 'utf8'), path)\n    return {\n      name: skillName, description,\n      invocation: { modelInvocable: true, userInvocable: true },\n      provider: 'dsh-office', source: 'bundled', rank: BUNDLED_SKILL_RANK,\n      resourceBase: { kind: 'directory', path: directory.split(sep).join('/') }, locator: path,\n    }\n  })\n  const provider: SkillProvider = {\n    name: 'dsh-office',\n    list: () => Promise.resolve(candidates),\n    async get(candidate, options) {\n      const { rank: _rank, locator, ...summary } = candidate\n      const raw = await readFile(locator as string, { encoding: 'utf8', signal: options.signal })\n      const content = parseSkill(raw, locator as string).content\n        + (['office-render', 'office-recalculate', 'office-export-pdf'].includes(candidate.name) ? officeRuntime(config) : '')\n      return { ...summary, content }\n    },\n  }\n  ctx.skills.registerProvider(() => provider)\n}\n","tsconfig.json":"{\n  \"extends\": \"../../../tsconfig.base.json\",\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"rootDir\": \"src\",\n    \"outDir\": \"lib/types\"\n  },\n  \"include\": [\n    \"src\"\n  ],\n  \"references\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"../../../vendor/cosmokit\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"../../../vendor/cordis\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"../../../vendor/schemastery\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"../skill\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","tests/skill-office.spec.ts":"import { cp, mkdtemp, readFile, rm, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises'\nimport { tmpdir } from 'node:os'\nimport { join, sep } from 'node:path'\nimport { fileURLToPath, pathToFileURL } from 'node:url'\nimport { Context } from '@deepseek-ai/cordis'\nimport Loader from '@deepseek-ai/cordis-plugin-loader'\nimport Include from '@deepseek-ai/cordis-plugin-include'\nimport SkillRegistry from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill'\nimport * as SkillOffice from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill-office'\nimport { isSea } from 'node:sea'\nimport { execa } from 'execa'\nimport { describe, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest'\n\nvi.mock('node:sea', () => ({ isSea: vi.fn(() => false) }))\n\nconst assets = fileURLToPath(new URL('../assets/', import.meta.url))\nconst names = ['office', 'office-docx', 'office-export-pdf', 'office-pptx', 'office-recalculate', 'office-render', 'office-xlsx']\n\ndescribe('bundled Office skills', () => {\n  it('keeps routing and authoring within the progressive context budgets', async () => {\n    const ctx = new Context()\n    try {\n      await ctx.plugin(SkillRegistry)\n      await ctx.plugin(SkillOffice)\n      const catalog = await ctx.skills.list()\n      expect(catalog.map(skill => skill.name)).toEqual(names)\n      const route = (await ctx.skills.get('office'))!\n      expect(Math.ceil(route.description.length / 4)).toBeLessThanOrEqual(50)\n      expect(Math.ceil(route.content.length / 4)).toBeLessThanOrEqual(200)\n      for (const [name, previousTokens] of [['office-docx', 1688], ['office-pptx', 1879], ['office-xlsx', 2330]] as const) {\n        const skill = (await ctx.skills.get(name))!\n        expect(Math.ceil(skill.content.length / 4)).toBeLessThanOrEqual(Math.floor(previousTokens * 0.65))\n        expect(skill.content).not.toMatch(/read_image|transparent|DPI/)\n        expect(skill.content).not.toContain('dsoffice')\n        expect(skill.content).toContain('office-render')\n      }\n    } finally { await ctx.fiber.dispose() }\n  })\n\n  it('loads each packaged body and removes all candidates on disposal', async () => {\n    const ctx = new Context()\n    try {\n      await ctx.plugin(SkillRegistry)\n      const fiber = await ctx.plugin(SkillOffice)\n      const catalog = await ctx.skills.list()\n      expect(catalog.map(skill => skill.name)).toEqual(names)\n      for (const skill of catalog) {\n        expect(skill.description.length).toBeLessThanOrEqual(500)\n        expect(skill).toMatchObject({ source: 'bundled', provider: 'dsh-office', invocation: { modelInvocable: true, userInvocable: true } })\n        const loaded = await ctx.skills.get(skill.name)\n        expect(loaded?.resourceBase).toEqual({ kind: 'directory', path: join(assets, skill.name).split(sep).join('/') })\n        const raw = await readFile(join(assets, skill.name, 'SKILL.md'), 'utf8')\n        const body = raw.replace(/^---\\r?\\n[\\s\\S]*?\\r?\\n---\\r?\\n/u, '').trim()\n        expect(loaded?.content.startsWith(body)).toBe(true)\n        if (!['office-render', 'office-recalculate', 'office-export-pdf'].includes(skill.name)) expect(loaded?.content).toBe(body)\n      }\n      await fiber.dispose()\n      expect(await ctx.skills.list()).toEqual([])\n    } finally {\n      await ctx.fiber.dispose()\n    }\n  })\n\n  it('loads relocated resources through a real cordis.yml composition', async () => {\n    const root = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'dsh-office-skills-'))\n    const ctx = new Context()\n    try {\n      const external = join(root, '中文 assets')\n      await cp(assets, external, { recursive: true })\n      const configPath = join(root, 'cordis.yml')\n      await writeFile(configPath, [\n        \"- name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill'\",\n        \"- name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill-office'\",\n        '  config:',\n        `    assetRoot: ${JSON.stringify(external)}`,\n        '',\n      ].join('\\n'))\n      ctx.baseUrl = pathToFileURL(root).href + '/'\n      await ctx.plugin(Loader)\n      ctx.loader.builtins.include = Include\n      const modules = new Map<string, unknown>([\n        ['@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill', SkillRegistry],\n        ['@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill-office', SkillOffice],\n      ])\n      ctx.loader.internal = {\n        version: 'v2',\n        loadCache: new Map(),\n        register() { throw new Error('unexpected register') },\n        getOrCreateModuleJob() { throw new Error('unexpected module job') },\n        resolveSync() { throw new Error('unexpected resolution') },\n        load() { throw new Error('unexpected load') },\n        async import(specifier: string) {\n          if (!modules.has(specifier)) throw new Error(`Unexpected Loader import: ${specifier}`)\n          return modules.get(specifier)\n        },\n      }\n      await ctx.loader.create({ name: 'cordis:include', config: { path: pathToFileURL(configPath).href } })\n      await ctx.loader.await()\n      expect((await ctx.skills.list()).map(skill => skill.name)).toEqual(names)\n      const loaded = await ctx.skills.get('office-xlsx')\n      expect(loaded?.resourceBase).toEqual({ kind: 'directory', path: join(external, 'office-xlsx').split(sep).join('/') })\n      const raw = await readFile(join(external, 'office-xlsx', 'SKILL.md'), 'utf8')\n      const body = raw.replace(/^---\\r?\\n[\\s\\S]*?\\r?\\n---\\r?\\n/u, '').trim()\n      expect(loaded?.content).toBe(body)\n    } finally {\n      await ctx.fiber.dispose()\n      await rm(root, { recursive: true, force: true })\n    }\n  })\n\n  it.each([\n    ['description: \"Quoted: description\"', '\\r\\n', 'Quoted: description'],\n    ['description: >-\\n  Folded\\n  description', '\\n', 'Folded description'],\n  ])('parses frontmatter %s and leaves body metadata-like lines intact', async (header, newline, description) => {\n    const root = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'dsh-office-metadata-'))\n    const ctx = new Context()\n    try {\n      await cp(assets, root, { recursive: true })\n      const body = '# Office instructions\\n\\ndescription: instruction text'\n      await writeFile(join(root, 'office-docx', 'SKILL.md'), `---\\n${header}\\n---\\n\\n${body}\\n`.replaceAll('\\n', newline))\n      await ctx.plugin(SkillRegistry)\n      await ctx.plugin(SkillOffice, { assetRoot: root })\n      const skill = await ctx.skills.get('office-docx')\n      expect(skill?.description).toBe(description)\n      expect(skill?.content).toBe(body.replaceAll('\\n', newline))\n    } finally {\n      await ctx.fiber.dispose()\n      await rm(root, { recursive: true, force: true })\n    }\n  })\n\n  it('rejects relative resource paths and incomplete asset trees before registration', async () => {\n    const root = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'dsh-office-invalid-'))\n    const ctx = new Context()\n    try {\n      await ctx.plugin(SkillRegistry)\n      expect(() => { SkillOffice.apply(ctx, { assetRoot: 'assets' }) }).toThrow('absolute directory')\n      await cp(assets, root, { recursive: true })\n      await rm(join(root, 'office-docx', 'SKILL.md'))\n      expect(() => { SkillOffice.apply(ctx, { assetRoot: root }) }).toThrow('SKILL.md')\n      await writeFile(join(root, 'office-docx', 'SKILL.md'), '# Missing frontmatter\\ndescription: body text\\n')\n      expect(() => { SkillOffice.apply(ctx, { assetRoot: root }) }).toThrow('has no YAML frontmatter')\n      for (const header of ['', 'null', 'scalar', 'name: office-docx', 'description: 3', 'description: \"\"']) {\n        await writeFile(join(root, 'office-docx', 'SKILL.md'), `---\\n${header}\\n---\\n# Instructions\\n`)\n        expect(() => { SkillOffice.apply(ctx, { assetRoot: root }) }).toThrow('has no description')\n      }\n      expect(await ctx.skills.list()).toEqual([])\n    } finally {\n      await ctx.fiber.dispose()\n      await rm(root, { recursive: true, force: true })\n    }\n  })\n})\n\nit('executes capabilities using only paths returned by the loaded skill from a separate workspace', async () => {\n  const root = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'office CLI 工作目录 '))\n  const ctx = new Context()\n  try {\n    await ctx.plugin(SkillRegistry)\n    await ctx.plugin(SkillOffice)\n    const skill = await ctx.skills.get('office-render')\n    const json = skill?.content.match(/\\n(\\{\\n[\\s\\S]+)$/u)?.[1]\n    expect(json).toBeDefined()\n    const { libreofficeKit } = JSON.parse(json!) as { libreofficeKit: { node: string; cli: string } }\n    const result = await execa(libreofficeKit.node, [libreofficeKit.cli, 'capabilities'], {\n      cwd: root, env: { PATH: '' }, timeout: 20_000, killSignal: 'SIGKILL', reject: false,\n    })\n    expect(result.timedOut, result.stderr).toBe(false)\n    expect(result.signal, result.stderr).toBeUndefined()\n    expect(result.exitCode, result.stderr).toBe(0)\n    expect(JSON.parse(result.stdout)).toMatchObject({ runtime: { version: '0.1.5', cliPath: libreofficeKit.cli } })\n  } finally {\n    await ctx.fiber.dispose()\n    await rm(root, { recursive: true, force: true })\n  }\n})\n\n\nit('validates operation paths on loading while authoring remains available', async () => {\n  const ctx = new Context()\n  const original = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(process.versions, 'electron')\n  try {\n    await ctx.plugin(SkillRegistry)\n    for (const config of [{ node: 'node' }, { cli: 'cli.js' }, { node: assets }, { cli: assets }, { cli: join(assets, 'missing.js') }]) {\n      const fiber = await ctx.plugin(SkillOffice, config)\n      expect((await ctx.skills.get('office-docx'))?.content).toContain('python-docx')\n      await expect(ctx.skills.get('office-render')).rejects.toThrow()\n      await fiber.dispose()\n    }\n    const carrier = await ctx.plugin(SkillOffice)\n    vi.mocked(isSea).mockReturnValue(true)\n    await expect(ctx.skills.get('office-render')).rejects.toThrow('standalone Node')\n    vi.mocked(isSea).mockReturnValue(false)\n    Object.defineProperty(process.versions, 'electron', { value: '44.0.0', configurable: true })\n    await expect(ctx.skills.get('office-render')).rejects.toThrow('standalone Node')\n    await carrier.dispose()\n    const disabled = await ctx.plugin(SkillOffice, { cli: false })\n    expect((await ctx.skills.get('office-render'))?.content).toContain('disabled in this deployment')\n    await disabled.dispose()\n    await ctx.plugin(SkillOffice, { node: process.execPath })\n    expect((await ctx.skills.get('office-render'))?.content).toContain(JSON.stringify(process.execPath))\n  } finally {\n    vi.mocked(isSea).mockReturnValue(false)\n    if (original === undefined) Reflect.deleteProperty(process.versions, 'electron')\n    else Object.defineProperty(process.versions, 'electron', original)\n    await ctx.fiber.dispose()\n  }\n})\n","tests/progressive-loading.spec.ts":"/** Model request contents for independent Office authoring and operation skills. */\nimport { afterEach, expect, it } from 'vitest'\nimport { Context } from '@deepseek-ai/cordis'\nimport AgentRegistry, { type Agent } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent'\nimport AgentLoop from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent-loop'\nimport { provideWorkingDirectoryFixture } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent-loop-testkit'\nimport LlmRuntime, { createUserMessage } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm'\nimport SessionStore, { SessionId } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-session'\nimport SessionProjectionRegistry from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-projection'\nimport SystemPrompt from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-system-prompt'\nimport ToolRuntime from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools'\nimport { PtcRuntime, type PtcRunRequest, type PtcRunSpec } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-ptc-runtime'\nimport SkillRegistry from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill'\nimport * as ToolSkill from '../../tool-skill/src/index.ts'\nimport * as SkillOffice from '../src/index.ts'\nimport { MockAdapter, textResponse, toolCallResponse } from '../../../core/agent-loop/tests/mock-adapter.ts'\n\nconst contexts: Context[] = []\nafterEach(async () => { for (const ctx of contexts.splice(0)) await ctx.fiber.dispose() })\n\nclass SkillProgram extends PtcRuntime {\n  readonly language = 'typescript'\n  readonly isolation = 'fixture'\n  resolve(request: PtcRunRequest): PtcRunSpec { return { ...request, cwd: process.cwd(), timeoutMs: 120_000 } }\n  async run(request: PtcRunSpec) {\n    return { logs: [], value: await request.bindings[0]!.functions.skill!({ name: request.program }) }\n  }\n}\n\nasync function setup(mode: 'native' | 'ptc', names: string[]) {\n  const ctx = new Context()\n  contexts.push(ctx)\n  provideWorkingDirectoryFixture(ctx)\n  await ctx.plugin(LlmRuntime)\n  await ctx.plugin(SessionStore)\n  await ctx.plugin(SessionProjectionRegistry)\n  await ctx.plugin(SystemPrompt, { personaPrefix: '', personaSuffix: '' })\n  await ctx.plugin(ToolRuntime, { mode })\n  await ctx.plugin(AgentRegistry)\n  await ctx.plugin(AgentLoop, { agents: [] })\n  await ctx.plugin(SkillRegistry)\n  await ctx.plugin(ToolSkill)\n  await ctx.plugin(SkillOffice)\n  if (mode === 'ptc') await ctx.plugin(SkillProgram)\n  const adapter = new MockAdapter([\n    ...names.map((name, index) => mode === 'native'\n      ? toolCallResponse(`skill-${index}`, 'skill', { name })\n      : toolCallResponse(`skill-${index}`, 'run_code', { code: name, description: 'Load task instructions' })),\n    textResponse('Done.'), textResponse('Continued.'), textResponse('Fork continued.'),\n  ])\n  ctx.llm.registerAdapter(['mock'], adapter)\n  const { agent } = await ctx.agents.create({ sessionId: SessionId('progressive-office'), agentOptions: { provider: 'mock', model: 'model' } })\n  return { ctx, agent, adapter }\n}\n\nasync function send(agent: Agent, text = 'Continue the task'): Promise<void> {\n  agent.followup(createUserMessage({ content: [{ type: 'text', text }], source: { kind: 'user' } }))\n  await agent.whenIdle()\n}\n\nit.each(['native', 'ptc'] as const)('loads the router and authoring body in %s; resume and fork retain those instructions', async (mode) => {\n  const { ctx, agent, adapter } = await setup(mode, ['office', 'office-docx'])\n  await send(agent, 'Edit the Word document text.')\n  expect(adapter.requests).toHaveLength(3)\n  const requests = adapter.requests.map(request => JSON.stringify(request))\n  expect(requests[0]).toContain('Create, edit, inspect, or convert Office')\n  expect(requests[0]).toContain('office-docx')\n  expect(requests[1]).toContain('Office task routing')\n  expect(requests[1]).not.toContain('python-docx')\n  expect(requests[2]).toContain('python-docx')\n  if (mode === 'ptc') {\n    expect(agent.session.snapshotEvents().filter(event => event.type === 'user/message' && event.data.source.kind === 'skill-invocation')).toEqual([])\n  }\n  expect(requests[2]).toContain('office-render')\n  expect(requests[2]).not.toContain('dsoffice')\n  expect(requests[0]).not.toContain('dsoffice')\n  expect(requests[1]).not.toContain('dsoffice')\n  for (const request of requests) {\n    expect(request).not.toMatch(/uniformly blank|fragment rectangles/)\n  }\n  const seed = agent.session.snapshotEvents()\n  const { agent: resumed } = await ctx.agents.create({ sessionId: SessionId('resumed-office'), agentOptions: { provider: 'mock', model: 'model' }, seed })\n  await send(resumed)\n  const { agent: forked } = await ctx.agents.create({ sessionId: SessionId('forked-office'), agentOptions: { provider: 'mock', model: 'model' }, seed, meta: { parentSession: agent.id } })\n  await send(forked)\n  for (const request of adapter.requests.slice(3)) {\n    const text = JSON.stringify(request)\n    expect(text).toContain('python-docx')\n    expect(text).toContain('office-render')\n    expect(text).not.toContain('dsoffice')\n    expect(text).not.toMatch(/uniformly blank|fragment rectangles/)\n  }\n  expect(agent.session.snapshotEvents()).toEqual(seed)\n})\n\nit.each(['office-render', 'office-recalculate', 'office-export-pdf'])('loads %s directly without unrelated operation or authoring bodies', async (name) => {\n  const { agent, adapter } = await setup('native', [name])\n  await send(agent)\n  const loaded = JSON.stringify(adapter.requests.at(-1))\n  expect(loaded).toContain('libreofficeKit')\n  expect(loaded).not.toContain('Office task routing')\n  expect(loaded).not.toContain('# Word documents')\n  if (name !== 'office-render') expect(loaded).not.toMatch(/render --input|uniformly blank|fragment rectangles|DPI/)\n  if (name !== 'office-recalculate') expect(loaded).not.toContain('recalculate --input')\n  if (name !== 'office-export-pdf') expect(loaded).not.toContain('convert --input')\n})\n\nit('loads an explicitly invoked authoring skill without the router', async () => {\n  const { agent, adapter } = await setup('native', [])\n  await send(agent, '/office-xlsx Change A1 to 42.')\n  expect(adapter.requests).toHaveLength(1)\n  const text = JSON.stringify(adapter.requests[0])\n  expect(text).toContain('# Excel workbooks')\n  expect(text).not.toMatch(/Office task routing|dsoffice/)\n})\n"},"symbols":{"defs":[["vendor/cordis/src/context.ts",16,"interface","interface Context","@deepseek-ai/cordis"],["vendor/schemastery/src/index.ts",252,"type","type Schema<S = any, T = S, Mode extends SchemaMode = 'plain'> = Schemastery<S, T, Mode>","@deepseek-ai/schemastery"],["packages/skill/skill/src/index.ts",28,"const","const BUNDLED_SKILL_RANK","@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill"],["packages/skill/skill/src/index.ts",77,"interface","interface SkillCandidate extends SkillSummary","@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill"],["packages/skill/skill/src/index.ts",247,"interface","interface SkillProvider","@deepseek-ai/dsh-skill"]],"files":{"src/index.ts":{"e":[["Config",16,"interface"],["name",33,"const"],["inject",35,"const"],["apply",69,"function"]],"i":[["Context",8,0],["z",9,1],["BUNDLED_SKILL_RANK",10,2],["SkillCandidate",10,3],["SkillProvider",10,4]]}},"api":[["Config","packages/skill/skill-office/src/index.ts",16,"interface","interface Config",0,"dsh-v0.1.6-alpha.2",0],["name","packages/skill/skill-office/src/index.ts",33,"const","const name",0,"dsh-v0.1.6-alpha.2",0],["inject","packages/skill/skill-office/src/index.ts",35,"const","const inject",0,"dsh-v0.1.6-alpha.2",0],["apply","packages/skill/skill-office/src/index.ts",69,"function","function apply(ctx: Context, config: Config = {}): void",0,"dsh-v0.1.6-alpha.2",0]],"uses":{}}});
